<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The herding folk (docs/design/peoples.md; DESIGN.md "Rimfolk's peoples"; Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/): nomad herders
    who follow the grass with great herds and keep only seasonal camps. Neolithic, on the game's tribal parent: hides of
    every make, their caps, wraps and coats dyed russet, archers and spear-wardens (their kinds, below). Their caravans walk a herd of eight to fourteen beasts for sale along
    with their pack animals (the game brings a caravan's animals for sale with it), and they come half again as often as
    another people's. Their camps are round houses round a fire with pens (TownPlanDef Rimfolk_Plan_HerdCamp, their herd in
    the pens). They bring their drovers and shearers to the colony's land more often, and in the fall and winter they ask
    to graze a herd there (Rimfolk_Camp_WinterHerd), leaving a young beast of the herd at the gate after a stay that went
    well; the drove roads' world event comes for them likeliest. Their founding (the description): Tamsa, who walked the
    last forty head through the dry year to grass and back; herders count every beast at dusk because she did. What they
    honour, fear and say is in their template (on their card). They defend
    their camps and raid only when the colony has turned them hostile (raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve 0.5). Listed once
    among the world's peoples when a world is made, never required. Faith (Ideology): a fixed creed of the herd (VE Memes'
    nomad and elders where loaded), the animalist style. Kind of people (Biotech): seven in ten baseliners; yttakin, neanderthals,
    pigskins, Alpha Genes' animusen, Vanilla Races Expanded's boarskins and saurids, venators, wood elves and Awakened Apes'
    gorillas (gentle giants of the grazing).
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="TribeBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Herders</defName>
    <label>herding folk</label>
    <description>Nomad herders who follow the grass with their great herds, from the summer pastures to the winter valleys and back. They keep only seasonal camps of round houses and pens, and trade beasts, wool and hides wherever they pass.\n\nTheir ways began in the year the wells failed, when the camps of the plains sat down to eat their herds and wait. A herd girl named Tamsa walked the last forty head north through two hundred miles of dust to grass nobody believed in, and brought every one of them home alive the next spring; the camps that followed her never stopped moving. Herders still count every beast at dusk because she did, and a beast left behind on the road is a shame no herder lives down.\n\nThey say little and mean all of it, and when they are asked whether a thing is true they say "the grass will tell." They are generous to a fair host and hard on a thief, and their archers ride the edges of every herd. Each camp is kept by its elder.</description>
    <pawnSingular>herder</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>herders</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>first herder</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_Herders_Herder</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_Herders</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_HerdersTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/Herders</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/HerdersTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.66, 0.36, 0.20)</li>
      <li>(0.88, 0.58, 0.34)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <canSiege>false</canSiege>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
    <startingCountAtWorldCreation>1</startingCountAtWorldCreation>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>9999</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <configurationListOrderPriority>36</configurationListOrderPriority>
    <settlementGenerationWeight>0.6</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve Inherit="False">
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0.5)</li>
      </points>
    </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
    <xenotypeSet Inherit="False">
      <xenotypeChances>
        <Yttakin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.06</Yttakin>
        <Neanderthal MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.04</Neanderthal>
        <Pigskin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.03</Pigskin>
        <AG_Animusen MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,sarg.alphagenes">0.04</AG_Animusen>
        <VRE_Boarskin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,vanillaracesexpanded.pigskin">0.03</VRE_Boarskin>
        <DV_Venator MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,det.venators">0.03</DV_Venator>
        <DevDesigner_XenotypeWoodElves MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,DevDesigner.Elves.Continued">0.04</DevDesigner_XenotypeWoodElves>
        <VRESaurids_Saurid MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,vanillaracesexpanded.saurid">0.02</VRESaurids_Saurid>
        <Gorilla MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,OnlyMonkey.AwakenedApes">0.02</Gorilla>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Long Grass</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>The herd is the people's wealth and the grass is the herd's. A camp stays only as long as the grass does, a beast is never left behind on the road, and a guest at the fire eats from the same pot. Tamsa's count is kept at every dusk, every beast by name, and the elders are heard before anyone. Fields are for those who stay; the herders move on.</ideoDescription>
    <forcedMemes>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Rancher</li>
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_Nomad</li>
      <!-- The elders heard before anyone: Vanilla Ideology Expanded's elders. -->
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_Elders</li>
    </forcedMemes>
    <structureMemeWeights Inherit="False">
      <Structure_Animist MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">4</Structure_Animist>
      <Structure_TheistEmbodied MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">1</Structure_TheistEmbodied>
    </structureMemeWeights>
    <styles>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Animalist</li>
    </styles>
    <caravanTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Caravan_Herders_Herd</li>
      <li>Rimfolk_Caravan_Herders_Wool</li>
    </caravanTraderKinds>
    <visitorTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Visitor_Herders</li>
    </visitorTraderKinds>
    <baseTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Base_Herders</li>
    </baseTraderKinds>
    <pawnGroupMakers Inherit="False">
      <li>
        <!-- A fight: archers and spear-wardens -->
        <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Archer>10</Rimfolk_Herders_Archer>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Warden>8</Rimfolk_Herders_Warden>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Herder>2</Rimfolk_Herders_Herder>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Peaceful</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Herder>20</Rimfolk_Herders_Herder>
          <Tribal_Child MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">8</Tribal_Child>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Archer>6</Rimfolk_Herders_Archer>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Warden>4</Rimfolk_Herders_Warden>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- A caravan: their drover, many pack beasts, and a herd for sale walking with it (the trader's stock) -->
        <kindDef>Trader</kindDef>
        <traders>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Drover>1</Rimfolk_Herders_Drover>
        </traders>
        <carriers>
          <Muffalo>8</Muffalo>
          <Yak>6</Yak>
          <Dromedary>5</Dromedary>
          <Alpaca>4</Alpaca>
          <Horse>4</Horse>
          <Elephant>1</Elephant>
        </carriers>
        <guards>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Archer>10</Rimfolk_Herders_Archer>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Warden>8</Rimfolk_Herders_Warden>
        </guards>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Settlement</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Archer>10</Rimfolk_Herders_Archer>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Warden>8</Rimfolk_Herders_Warden>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Herder>10</Rimfolk_Herders_Herder>
          <Rimfolk_Herders_Elder>2</Rimfolk_Herders_Elder>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <kindDef>Hunters</kindDef>
        <commonality>1</commonality>
        <options>
          <Tribal_Hunter>1</Tribal_Hunter>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <kindDef>Loggers</kindDef>
        <commonality>1</commonality>
        <options>
          <Tribal_Logger>1</Tribal_Logger>
        </options>
      </li>
    </pawnGroupMakers>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="ColonyCouncil.PeopleExtension">
        <calling>herders</calling>
        <!-- Their age over the years (Peoples/PeopleAges.cs): close to the land and the herd, they rise late, and no further than the industrial age. -->
        <agePace>20</agePace>
        <ageLimit>2</ageLimit>
        <townWord>camp</townWord>
        <townWords>camps</townWords>
        <head>camp elder</head>
        <heir>second elder</heir>
        <envoy>rider</envoy>
        <trader>drover</trader>
        <courier>rider</courier>
        <couriers>riders</couriers>
        <caravanWeight>1.5</caravanWeight>
        <camps>
          <li>Council_Camp_Drovers</li>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_Shearers</li>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_Catchers</li>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_WinterHerd</li>
        </camps>
        <plan>Rimfolk_Plan_HerdCamp</plan>
        <honours>the count at dusk, a guest at the fire and good grass</honours>
        <fears>the dry year, the thief and a fence across the old drove roads</fears>
        <sayings>
          <li>Count them at dusk.</li>
          <li>Never leave a beast on the road.</li>
          <li>A guest eats from the same pot.</li>
          <li>The grass will tell.</li>
        </sayings>
        <townGoods>
          <Hay>120~240</Hay>
          <WoolSheep>40~90</WoolSheep>
          <Leather_Plain>30~70</Leather_Plain>
          <Pemmican>60~120</Pemmican>
          <MedicineHerbal>4~10</MedicineHerbal>
        </townGoods>
        <herd>
          <li>Muffalo</li>
          <li>Yak</li>
          <li>Sheep</li>
          <li>Goat</li>
          <li>Cow</li>
          <li>Alpaca</li>
          <li>Dromedary</li>
          <li>Horse</li>
        </herd>
        <herdCount>8~14</herdCount>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </FactionDef>

  <!-- ===================== Their people ===================== -->

  <!--
    How alike they look (docs/design/peoples.md "Their gear, their kinds of people and their gifts"): herders vary freely
    around their signature, russet on their caps and wraps (Ideology's tail caps and broadwraps, the war veil, the elder's
    headdress) and on whatever coat or poncho they wear over the hides; under it, the game's tribal gear and the mods'
    (Vanilla Apparel Expanded's kilts, ponchos and pelt coats, Vanilla Factions Expanded - Tribals' wraps) in their own
    leathers and colours; herders, drovers and the elder a lasso at the hip for the beasts (Melee Animation). Their herd
    wardens are their only fighters and wear one harness: the war veil, and Tribals' war wraps where it is loaded. Archers
    carry a quiver (Vanilla Apparel Expanded - Accessories). Slings, clubs, spears and bows of the game and the mods (Vanilla
    Weapons Expanded - Tribal's slings and clubs, Rimsenal's blowguns and throwing clubs, Tribals' stakes), the archers'
    javelins with Vanilla Factions Expanded - Classical, under the game's neolithic tags. They carry hay and hides, with
    Odyssey muskox wool, with Alpha Crafts butter. A few are A RimWorld of Magic's druids (their elder), rangers (their
    archers) or gladiators (their wardens). Without any mod: tribalwear, parkas, the war veil and the headdress, the base
    game's clubs, spears, ikwas and bows.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef Name="Rimfolk_HerdersKindBase" Abstract="True">
    <race>Human</race>
    <defaultFactionDef>Rimfolk_Herders</defaultFactionDef>
    <maxGenerationAge>70</maxGenerationAge>
    <chemicalAddictionChance>0.04</chemicalAddictionChance>
    <invNutrition>2.55</invNutrition>
    <invFoodDef>Pemmican</invFoodDef>
    <apparelTags>
      <li>Neolithic</li>
    </apparelTags>
    <specificApparelRequirements>
      <!-- Russet on the caps and wraps and on the coat over the hides, whichever they wear. -->
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_WarVeil</apparelDef><color>(0.70, 0.42, 0.24)</color></li>
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_TribalHeaddress</apparelDef><color>(0.70, 0.42, 0.24)</color></li>
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_Parka</apparelDef><color>(0.70, 0.42, 0.24)</color></li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology"><apparelDef>Apparel_Tailcap</apparelDef><color>(0.70, 0.42, 0.24)</color></li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology"><apparelDef>Apparel_Broadwrap</apparelDef><color>(0.70, 0.42, 0.24)</color></li>
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VAPPE"><apparelDef>VAE_Apparel_TribalPoncho</apparelDef><color>(0.70, 0.42, 0.24)</color></li>
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VAPPE"><apparelDef>VAE_Apparel_PeltCoat</apparelDef><color>(0.70, 0.42, 0.24)</color></li>
    </specificApparelRequirements>
  </PawnKindDef>

